# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Pengenalan {#introduction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The world is approaching the era of quantum advantage. Here, quantum advantage refers to executing a task on a hybrid quantum–classical system such that:\n"
"* The correctness of the output can be rigorously verified.\n"
"* The computation demonstrates a quantum separation &mdash; providing superior efficiency, cost-effectiveness, or accuracy compared with classical methods alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dunia sedang menghampiri era kelebihan kuantum. Di sini, kelebihan kuantum merujuk kepada pelaksanaan tugas pada sistem hibrid kuantum–klasik sedemikian rupa sehingga:\n"
"* Ketepatan output boleh disahkan secara ketat.\n"
"* Pengiraan menunjukkan pemisahan kuantum &mdash; memberikan kecekapan, keberkesanan kos, atau ketepatan yang lebih unggul berbanding kaedah klasik semata-mata.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reaching quantum advantage in the near term will require us to use every available tool to get the most out of today’s quantum hardware. In practice, that means confronting noise and errors head-on.\n"
"We have an ever-expanding toolkit to address these challenges, including error suppression, error mitigation, error detection, and error correction. These concepts can be difficult to distinguish, in part because they lie along a continuum on the path toward fault-tolerant quantum computing. Roughly speaking:\n"
"* Error suppression aims to reduce the probability of certain errors occurring in the first place.\n"
"* Error mitigation seeks to reduce the impact of errors that have occurred on the final result.\n"
"* Error detection and correction encode quantum information redundantly across multiple qubits, so that errors can be detected and corrected through consistency checks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mencapai kelebihan kuantum dalam jangka masa terdekat memerlukan kita menggunakan setiap alat yang ada untuk mendapatkan hasil optimum daripada perkakasan kuantum masa kini. Dalam praktiknya, ini bermakna kita perlu menangani hingar dan ralat secara terus.\n"
"Kita mempunyai set alat yang sentiasa berkembang untuk menangani cabaran ini, termasuk penindasan ralat, mitigasi ralat, pengesanan ralat, dan pembetulan ralat. Konsep-konsep ini boleh sukar dibezakan, sebahagiannya kerana ia berada dalam satu kontinum sepanjang laluan menuju pengkomputeran kuantum bertoleransi kerosakan. Secara kasarnya:\n"
"* Penindasan ralat bertujuan mengurangkan kebarangkalian ralat tertentu berlaku pada mulanya.\n"
"* Mitigasi ralat berusaha mengurangkan kesan ralat yang telah berlaku terhadap hasil akhir.\n"
"* Pengesanan dan pembetulan ralat mengekod maklumat kuantum secara berlebihan merentasi berbilang qubit, supaya ralat dapat dikesan dan dibetulkan melalui pemeriksaan konsistensi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Image of errors being reduced by error suppression, then correction, then mitigation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/intro/error-handling.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Image of errors being reduced by error suppression, then correction, then mitigation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/intro/error-handling.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some techniques blur these boundaries. For example, if errors can be detected at the circuit level and invalid shots are discarded or probabilistically recovered in post-processing, this may be viewed as a limited form of error correction, though it lacks the full fault-tolerant structure of quantum error-correcting codes.\n"
msgstr "Sesetengah teknik mengaburkan sempadan ini. Sebagai contoh, jika ralat dapat dikesan pada peringkat litar dan shot yang tidak sah dibuang atau dipulihkan secara kebarangkalian semasa pasca-pemprosesan, ini boleh dilihat sebagai satu bentuk terhad pembetulan ralat, walaupun ia tidak mempunyai struktur bertoleransi kerosakan yang penuh seperti kod pembetulan ralat kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling, another example, reshapes noise so that it behaves like a stochastic Pauli process. This can slow the buildup of coherent errors and make other techniques, such as error mitigation, more effective. On its own, however, it is best described as a form of noise tailoring, rather than strictly suppression or mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling, contoh lain, membentuk semula hingar supaya ia berkelakuan seperti proses Pauli stokastik. Ini boleh melambatkan pengumpulan ralat koheren dan menjadikan teknik lain, seperti mitigasi ralat, lebih berkesan. Namun begitu, dengan sendirinya, ia lebih tepat digambarkan sebagai satu bentuk penyesuaian hingar, bukannya penindasan atau mitigasi secara ketat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These tools are not mutually exclusive. Effective workflows often combine multiple approaches. Suppression and mitigation are widely applicable today, while error detection can be used in some workflows to discard erroneous results or probabilistically recover correct states. Meanwhile, increasingly advanced forms of error correction are steadily coming within reach. By leveraging and combining these methods, we can build a continuous path toward fault-tolerant quantum computing. For a streamlined approach to leveraging multiple error mitigation techniques, without much theoretical background, see [this tutorial](/tutorials/combine-error-mitigation-techniques) on IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"
msgstr "Alat-alat ini tidak saling eksklusif. Aliran kerja yang berkesan sering menggabungkan pelbagai pendekatan. Penindasan dan mitigasi boleh digunakan secara meluas pada masa kini, manakala pengesanan ralat boleh digunakan dalam sesetengah aliran kerja untuk membuang hasil yang salah atau memulihkan keadaan yang betul secara kebarangkalian. Sementara itu, bentuk pembetulan ralat yang semakin canggih semakin mudah dicapai. Dengan memanfaatkan dan menggabungkan kaedah-kaedah ini, kita boleh membina laluan berterusan menuju pengkomputeran kuantum bertoleransi kerosakan. Untuk pendekatan yang mudah bagi memanfaatkan pelbagai teknik mitigasi ralat, tanpa banyak latar belakang teori, lihat [tutorial ini](/tutorials/combine-error-mitigation-techniques) di IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this course, Tools for Quantum Advantage, we will explore some of the most promising methods for managing quantum noise and errors. Our focus is on exploring practical applications using Qiskit, while providing enough theoretical background to help you determine which techniques are appropriate for your use case. We will also highlight which methods can be combined effectively within a single workflow &mdash; and which ones typically cannot.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kursus ini, Alat untuk Kelebihan Kuantum, kita akan meneroka beberapa kaedah paling menjanjikan bagi menguruskan hingar dan ralat kuantum. Fokus kita adalah meneroka aplikasi praktikal menggunakan Qiskit, sambil menyediakan latar belakang teori yang mencukupi untuk membantu anda menentukan teknik mana yang sesuai untuk kes penggunaan anda. Kita juga akan menonjolkan kaedah mana yang boleh digabungkan secara berkesan dalam satu aliran kerja &mdash; dan mana yang biasanya tidak boleh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Join us as we explore the tools that will help bring quantum advantage within reach.\n"
msgstr "Sertai kami semasa kita meneroka alat-alat yang akan membantu membawa kelebihan kuantum semakin hampir.\n"
